From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ios-blink-sideload <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:39:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS sideload: find in page

Find in Page was disabled: Chrome asks the web state whether it can be
searched, and ContentWebState said no (IsFindInteractionSupported() and
the rest were stubs). With WKWebView, Chrome uses the web view's system
find navigator (UIFindInteraction).

Give the Blink web view the same system find navigator, with a find
session (a UIFindSession subclass) that searches through content's find
(WebContents::Find, StopFinding). Blink highlights the matches and
scrolls to the active one; its replies (DidReceiveFindReply) give the
navigator the match count and which match is active. Blink finds
substrings only, so the navigator's Whole Words option is removed;
Match Case works.

Status: verified at Chromium 4558926c in the iOS 27 simulator: Chrome's
"Find in Page" menu item is enabled and shows the system find navigator
above the on-screen keyboard; "apple" on a test page shows 1/5 with all
five matches highlighted and the first one active, as in Safari on the
same simulator (both show 2/5 when the word is typed with the Pinyin
keyboard and committed from its candidate bar: committing the same text
moves to the next match); Next and Previous
move through the matches, scrolling to each, and wrap from 5/5 to 1/5;
Match Case leaves 1/4; a word that is not on the page shows 0; a
Chinese word typed with the Pinyin keyboard is found; closing the
navigator clears the highlights, and Find opens again afterwards.

